Package: linkrd
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: systemd
Description: USB ACM text clipboard synchronization agent for Linkr
 Linkrd synchronizes the UTF-8 plain-text clipboard of a desktop user
 session with a Radxa Linkr device over a USB CDC-ACM serial port. It
 monitors clipboard changes, performs periodic refreshes, deduplicates
 repeated content, prevents feedback loops, acknowledges writes, sends
 heartbeats, and reconnects automatically when the device disappears.
 .
 Only plain text is synchronized; images, files, and chunked transfers are
 not implemented. Clipboard access works on Wayland and X11.
 .
 The package installs /usr/bin/linkrd, a udev rule that grants the logged-in
 desktop user access to the Linkr USB device, and a systemd user unit. The
 user unit is installed but not enabled; enable it once per user with
 "systemctl --user daemon-reload" and "systemctl --user enable --now
 linkrd.service".
 .
 Do not use "linkrd install --autostart" together with this package: that
 command installs a private executable copy in the user's home directory
 which package upgrades cannot update. See /usr/share/doc/linkrd/ for
 details.
